; The fetch stack (P6): URL fetching behind the Net authority grant, the
; extraction-backend contract, and the JSON/table renderers a page can take.
; It is its own library — [seekwright.fetch], wrapped as [Seekwright_fetch] —
; the way [lib/providers/] is [seekwright.providers], because the dependency
; direction is fixed the same way: nothing in [lib/] may name a fetch backend,
; so whatever builds one (the engine, P5, or the factory) depends on this
; library, never the reverse.
;
; All HTTP goes through a [Mcp_caps.Authority.Net] grant — no raw cohttp — and
; the fetcher receives the grant plus the extraction backend injected, with no
; default backend, so importing this library never imports a backend's
; dependencies. The page cache ([page_cache.ml], F7) is in this library because
; a cached window is cut with [Fetcher.window_text], and the cut has to be one
; function rather than a mirror kept true by a test.
;
; The stdlib extraction backend sits in [extractors/] with its own stanza
; ([seekwright.fetch.stdlib]) for the same reason [lib/providers/] has one:
; a backend is a separate install unit, and [extractors/] is where the next one
; lands without the fetcher naming it.
(library
 (name seekwright_fetch)
 (public_name seekwright.fetch)
 ; [seekwright.text] is the one codepoint walk (style review H1/H2) and
 ; [seekwright.wire] the page records this library produces and [seekwright]
 ; consumes: both used to own a copy, and the layer between the two libraries
 ; copied the record field by field. Neither big library may link the other, so
 ; both sit on a stdlib-only floor under both. [eio] is the chain budget on
 ; [Fetcher.fetch] (quality review, fetch finding 4) — a timeout value, not a
 ; clock: the caller holds the monotonic clock — and the loop side of
 ; [Extract_pool]; [unix] is the worker side of that pool only: the extraction
 ; workers speak plain Unix syscalls on an AF_UNIX socket precisely so they
 ; never enter the loop's domain (plans/ocaml-finalisation.md, F2.2).
 ; [digestif] is the page cache's entry key: the file name is a hash of the route
 ; rung and the validated URL, so a model-supplied URL never becomes a path.
 (libraries
  seekwright.text
  seekwright.wire
  mcp-caps
  uri
  ipaddr
  yojson
  eio
  digestif
  unix))
